                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_59\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit adds a `destroy(Context)` method to `DownloadManagerInterface` (which unregisters `downloadCompletionReceiver` and clears the singleton `instance`) and calls it from `MainActivity.onDestroy()`. This addresses a resource leak: `DownloadManagerInterface.init()` calls `registerReceiver()`, which registers a `BroadcastReceiver` with the application context, but nothing ever unregisters it or tears down the singleton.\n\nCandidate_59 is the commit that created this exact situation. It:\n1. Deletes the old `DownloadManagerAsyncTask`/`NewsletterDownloadHelper` classes and the old `MainActivity` receiver logic, which previously included an `onDestroy()` that called `unregisterReceiver(downloadCompletionReceiver)` \u2014 i.e. it removed the code path that used to clean up a receiver.\n2. Introduces the new `DownloadManagerInterface` class (in `.../data/DownloadManagerInterface.java`) with a `registerReceiver()` method that registers `downloadCompletionReceiver` via `context.registerReceiver(...)`, called from the new `init()` method (invoked once from `SebApp.onCreate()`).\n3. Does NOT add any corresponding teardown/destroy logic \u2014 no `unregisterReceiver` call and no `onDestroy` override in `MainActivity` referencing `DownloadManagerInterface`.\n\nThis is precisely the gap the fix commit later closes: it adds the missing `destroy(Context)` method to `DownloadManagerInterface` and wires it into `MainActivity.onDestroy()`. Since candidate_59 is the commit that first introduced the receiver registration without any matching disposal mechanism, it is the bug-introducing commit. No candidate prior to 59 contains `DownloadManagerInterface` at all (grep for `DownloadManagerInterface` across all candidates only matches 59 through 67), and candidates 60-66 only modify unrelated behavior of the same class without adding any destroy/unregister logic (only candidate_67, which is identical to the fix diff itself, finally adds it).\n"
